[B]About[/B]

This is the stock firmware of the [B]Huawei Y220-U05[/B] packed as a ZIP that installs from TWRP. Use it to go back to stock from a custom ROM (for example CyanogenMod 7) without SP Flash Tool.

[LIST]
[*]Build: [B]Y220-U05V100R001C482B206[/B]
[*]Android 2.3.6 Gingerbread, build date 2014-01-12
[*]Stock kernel and stock boot image
[*][B]Rooted[/B]: su and Superuser are included, as in the original backup
[/LIST]

The ZIP was made from a TWRP backup of a stock phone. Every file, owner, permission (setuid included) and symlink comes from that backup; the 881 system files are byte-identical to it.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only for Huawei Y220-U05. It is not compatible with Huawei Y210 or other MT6572 phones.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]What it does[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Empties the existing /system UBIFS volume and copies the stock system
[*]Writes the stock boot image (kernel and ramdisk)
[*]Does [B]not[/B] touch data, cache, recovery (TWRP stays), NVRAM, IMEI or the modem partitions
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Tested[/B][/SIZE]

On a real Y220-U05 with TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 (2026-10-21): installs in about 46 seconds with no errors, boots to the stock launcher, and the SIM registers on the network. Going back to CyanogenMod 7 afterwards with a TWRP restore also worked.

[SIZE="4"][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][URL="https://xdaforums.com/t/recovery-unofficial-twrp-3-1-1-0-1-for-huawei-y220-u05.4805984/"]TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 for Huawei Y220-U05[/URL] (use the 2026-10-21 build or newer)
[*]A microSD card with at least 200 MB free
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Make a full TWRP backup to the microSD first.[/B][/COLOR]

[LIST=1]
[*]Copy the ZIP to the external microSD and check its MD5.
[*]Boot into TWRP.
[*][B]Wipe → Data and Cache.[/B] This is required when coming from a custom ROM; its data does not work on stock.
[*]Install the ZIP.
[*]Reboot to system. The first boot takes a few minutes.
[/LIST]

USB debugging is off after a clean install. Turn it on in [B]Settings → Applications → Development[/B] if you need ADB.

